{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_0759237a21392774e6189540bbee5ad73a6b9e610d8d5c92cf7012e4220ca685","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_896379b8c2bc7a14eb7496609de0dfaf81883419bb38c83fdf6348c010f4eefd"],"source_ids":["src_9e77a5d7b541592e95574337e0939676"],"text":"Six knowledge types (LEARNED, DECISION, FACT, PATTERN, INVESTIGATION, DEVIATION) are captured inline during work, and relevant entries are recalled automatically at session start based on current beads and the git branch.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2ba14b166d28f5a00d26af2ceef2efe4ff1a2a37afed8f5951009e7b5e50f760","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_364e4c21ea637121fa72ff44b6e8aa8ffa7eb94731c9b86925f9ad1a6cb8d93c","slc_46ca50a92604397c992288c8d7672bd5e70a738cbdba7a5e68f7c6027142f449"],"source_ids":["src_35567bae24cc5af0ad133d7616335a0b"],"text":"The docs acknowledge autonomous-mode trade-offs: bash runs without review, file writes are unapproved with only advisory ownership enforcement, and there is no human checkpoint; mitigations include feature branches, low retry budgets, and worktree/container isolation.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_324cc7c5b1f0dbb27e19261818620eff197ec378cbebffd88d48089893509bdc","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2893d99a91307f6266b5a8d0dcf189c9d1157b21b10a9bcfac93626a9d292f1b","slc_4c4a55f4477cf4b75b77cb67d757b287a6e8acec4c4275352af87929359bfc6b","slc_cee3f43d0be849b9daaabf65a929e3f9523aa923cd9a8150e937b886c0919eeb","slc_fcb7d7819740b13c2134564381113ac661dd92d9aac3b7df775250302dafc616"],"source_ids":["src_9e77a5d7b541592e95574337e0939676","src_9e7b56e7670d50f19d2dddb570627aab"],"text":"/lavra-work auto-routes between single-bead and multi-bead parallel execution, with a configurable max_parallel_agents (default 3) and per-task atomic commits whose bead IDs make git log grep useful.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3a585a3901557192b9c72fece8243a642d4be055681b4bf0dcd8021c2b202cc0","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=evaluation","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14d474fc17c6555d41057ea89292b5fdad35d0f536fc8eaa0eae0366bfdef17d"],"source_ids":["src_cd9b9ee0e3a0502880efbc7045a89629"],"text":"The architecture doc reports FTS5 search with BM25 ranking improved precision by 18%, recall by 17%, and MRR by 24% over grep-based search across 25 benchmark queries.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_51e4c4920a85e9d9d7259859ffb1bb9376dfe12e617d5468497e0504234c7a24","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=memory-state","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5b50170a835b9135fd887f9513ba923326d65cd2f9f4578b2bfa7c4a1613af07","slc_f3f8b4f26a2ddcb3a4da15c2af953439c92a5b276b9a0e8c85358ed8cc3095c1"],"source_ids":["src_cd9b9ee0e3a0502880efbc7045a89629"],"text":"Knowledge is stored in a shared append-only JSONL log (.lavra/memory/knowledge.jsonl) committed to git, with a local SQLite FTS5 search index, a curated active cache, and an audit log of sanitizer filtering actions.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_53fb2d98d15ce3f271d638fdbc0247d92e588684a9c6dc2d36530b39cfe3a834","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_67f877f1b4d3be9c493e167ee11befd7dc65eaf62520690153968f5fc279b961","slc_b1cc55d0811008e3fb2cf62d97e922a2730f8deb43bc83db1adc3253fc8315b5"],"source_ids":["src_9e77a5d7b541592e95574337e0939676","src_cd9b9ee0e3a0502880efbc7045a89629"],"text":"Lavra requires the beads CLI, jq, and sqlite3; the memory sanitizer compiles a Go helper when Go is available and falls back to a jq-based path otherwise, and grep-based search remains if sqlite3 is missing.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","created_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_5c1e51242568c4b9eb38a9fafccb8c353e3638f05a4d765141aef5b768ab1a54","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"roberto-mello/lavra@2e7e512eb90b snapshot 955fc447d95d4f9a","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_14d474fc17c6555d41057ea89292b5fdad35d0f536fc8eaa0eae0366bfdef17d","slc_6b7966d1d85882290c1678f11341c8e8bbf89058cb389461b1787cc4b30f76a5","slc_9bae9aef3b27bf632e4b4fd324830b5153f0888d06043ce150cca1a0a3709d72"],"source_ids":["src_9e77a5d7b541592e95574337e0939676","src_cd9b9ee0e3a0502880efbc7045a89629"],"text":"Lavra is a fork of Every's compound-engineering-plugin (MIT), replacing markdown knowledge storage with beads-based JSONL memory, FTS5 search, and workflows that create and update beads instead of markdown files.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T04:18:53Z","updated_by_operation":"op_57472a7e775e4d0c8921f7f19b41c239"}
